## Plotlines Pi5 QA/UAT elevation proxy — issue #450, companion to epic #264
## and to #304 (which built service/plotlines_service/elevation_proxy.py but
## never its deployment). See deploy/elevation/README.md.
##
## Deliberately its own Caddy instance and site block, never folded into
## deploy/mirror/'s Caddyfile — #304's own "Done when" named a separate
## hostname/port because the ToS/key-revocation risk here differs from the
## mirror's ODbL redistribution risk, so this must not inherit whatever
## issue #263 decides about the mirror's reachability.
##
## LAN-only, port-only address, no hostname: never bind this to a public DNS
## record. A bare `:PORT` address (unlike the mirror Caddyfile's
## `http://<host>`) has no domain name for Caddy to request a certificate
## for, so there is nothing to disable explicitly here the way the mirror's
## `http://` prefix has to.
##
## elevation-proxy has no auth of its own (see its own --host argparse help
## in service/plotlines_service/elevation_proxy.py) — Caddy publishing the
## only host-reachable port, with the elevation-proxy container publishing
## none (see docker-compose.yml), is what keeps it off the open LAN beyond
## "reachable to anyone already on this network," same posture as the
## mirror-clip container.

:{$ELEVATION_PORT:8090} {
	reverse_proxy elevation-proxy:8090

	log {
		output file {$ELEVATION_LOG:/var/log/caddy/elevation.log}
	}
}
